{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-adventure/1479456-tc-adventure-paths-before-the-aeon-society","id":1479456,"title":"[TC Adventure! ] Paths BEFORE the Aeon Society","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Adventure!"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-04-24T17:53:12-07:00","id":1479456,"title":"[TC Adventure! ] Paths BEFORE the Aeon Society","content":"So preparing my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1476045-adventure-aeon-society-creation-story\">'AEON Society creation story'</a>, I got a bit mental block on PCs part - If all Allegiances are created AFTER the Aeon Society - what characters that are funding members choose on charcter creation? \ud83e\udd14 PCs have Origin, Role and Society Paths to choose.<br /> <br /> But all new Societies/Allegiances are created AFTER Aeon in 1923? So no Society Path... Or do Allegiances in TC Adventure! 2E were created before Aeon Society?<br /> <br /> Or maybe just let players create their own pseudo Societies? Like 'just pick a Path LIKE Allegiance - but this will be your individual characters contacts and experience - instead of proper Society you join'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-25-2022, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-24T19:25:14-07:00","id":1479463,"title":"","content":"Some of them should or could pre-date Aeon: Branch 9, IDA, Le Salon des Femmes Nouveaux, The Archivists, Lodestar (The Pharro's Lightkeepers), Invictus Umbra, The Pownatowski Foundation, The Dragon's Coil Tong (pre-cursor to the Seven Brothers). I know, some of those are bad guys. But there are some societies from the book active pre-Aeon. You could also have them take Aeon even before it exists because they are Aeon even before they knew it. Presumably the skills and abilities that made them founding members were things they already had and formed the blueprint for later members. You could also make up other societies that the PC's were connected to prior to forming Aeon (not too hard).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T06:41:55-07:00","id":1479485,"title":"","content":"I'd use what you learned creating the Thule Society Path for your villain to create a new Society Path for the PCs to share, if you want them to have some unified background. Slagheap is 100% correct about how a lot of the Societies should or could predate Aeon, even if the printed material disagrees I think for the campaign you have planned there isn't really a need to make Aeon the first one, since you are specifically telling the story of how Aeon is founded.<br /> <br /> If you want your players to come for a variety of groups your idea of using existing Origin and Role paths and re-skinning them for more mundane societies isn't a bad one. Every path has a society element in the form of what the Connections represent, so you'd really just be attaching that Path to a more formal organization. This option might work really well if you want to highlight the need for the Aeon society, where you have all these Inspired people struggling to work together despite divided loyalties, with Aeon forming to bring them together united towards a specific purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4270-literatzi","name":"literatzi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4270_2.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-25T12:43:18-07:00","id":1479499,"title":"","content":"Some secret societies might have died out before the twentieth century, others might have been destroyed or rendered obsolete in the horror of WWI. <br /> <br /> Occult focused societies would be highly fashionable in the late 1800s and even more highly risable by 1930.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-27T17:14:32-07:00","id":1479618,"title":"","content":"Les Fant\u00f4mes. Draw inspiration from period characters like AJ Raffles (1898), Arsene Lupin (1905), Hercule Flambeau (1910), Fantomas (1911), and Filibus (1915), as well as the real world Adam Worth (1844 - 1902), the main characters from Michael Crichton's The Great Train Robbery and (to a lesser degree) the characters from the manga/anime Moriarty the Patriot. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-29T17:46:47-07:00","id":1479765,"title":"","content":"I suppose if one is looking for the most archetypical societal groups from before the Great War (what Mutants &amp; Masterminds used to call the Gaslight Age, IIRC):<ul><li>Gentlemen Thieves (Les Fant\u00f4mes above)</li> <li>Gentlemen Detectives - counterparts to the above, Sherlock Holmes and his ilk</li> <li>The Explorers Club - Alan Quartermain, Prof. Challenger, etc.</li> <li>Scientific Fantastique - All of your various inventors, super scientists, etc.</li> <li>Spiritualists - Psychics, ghost hunters, etc. (who may or may not be part of the same group as ...)</li> <li>Quasi-Secret Society of Ritual Magician Occultists - Golden Dawn, Crowley, and so forth</li> <li>Proto-Technocrat Imperialists - firm leadership by the experts and elites</li> <li>Bohemian Aesthetics - Libertine romantics and hedonists</li> <li>Gothic Monster Hunters</li> </ul>That's just off the top of my head. Some of the preexisting groups probably have some degree of overlap with these on some level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T20:41:50-07:00","id":1487539,"title":"","content":"With <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/trinity-continuum-aether-tabletop-roleplaying-game\" target=\"_blank\"><b>TC Aether</b></a>, problem is self resolving. Before Max Mercer's <i>Aeon Society</i> that is more humanitarian exploration group for Inspired from 1923 - there was <i>Esoteric Order of Aeons </i>from 1882 that was egyptologists society going global and cross-cultural in Victorian era. ( Or 'S-F version of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mysterium\" target=\"_blank\"><b>MtAw</b> Mysterium</a>', as I like to sum them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) Where <i>Aeon Society</i> of 1920s is mainly altruistic, <i>Esoteric Order</i> is much more driven by the discovery of knowledge itself. None the less, in 1923 Max simply reform last remnants of eclectic <i>Order of Aeons</i> into new <i>Society</i>, mixing last few members of Order with new blood, more in line with his vision of Aeon - and so we got modern Aeon Society, and later, Aeon Group. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> / Mechanically, you can use for 'preAeon Aeon members', both <i>Esoteric Order</i> Path or <i>A</i><i>eon Society</i> Path - as they are already very much similar. /","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}